{# ── The winner's moment ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Include INSIDE the markup that already names the winner, so the celebration
   cannot outlive the thing it is celebrating — a held or delayed result renders
   no winner block, and therefore no include, and therefore no confetti.

   Usage:
     {% include 'partials/celebrate.twig' with { key: r.slug } only %}

   `key` makes it once-per-result rather than once-per-browser: somebody who
   reads three categories should see three celebrations, and somebody who
   reopens one should see a document.

   The page marks what to animate with two attributes and nothing else:
     data-celebrate="<key>"     on the wrapper
     data-celebrate-figure      the number to count up (optional)
     data-celebrate-anchor      what the second burst falls from (optional)

   Both scripts are DEFERRED and neither renders anything. If they never arrive
   the page is exactly the page: the name, the index and the breakdown are the
   server's output and nothing here reveals them. #}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" src="{{ asset('/assets/js/vendor/canvas-confetti-1.9.3.js') }}" defer></script>
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" src="{{ asset('/assets/js/celebrate.js') }}" defer></script>
